# Sample engine

Plain HTML, CSS, and vanilla JS (ES2018+). No framework and no activity build step. Load content with `<script src="content.js">` as `window.CONTENT`, not `fetch()`.

- `content.js` holds text, scores, and `next` ids. `app.js` holds the screen router.
- Shared files live in `shared/` and are copied by `scripts/sync-shared.mjs`. Edit the shared source, then sync.
- State stays in memory, with optional `sessionStorage`. Do not send data anywhere except the SCORM API.
- Feedback scenario: choices worth 10 / 5 / 0, max 30; endings 25–30, 15–20, 0–10; shuffle choices; no back button inside the scenario.
- Safety challenge: 100 base per question; +50 time bonus only if the timer is on and at least half the time remains; hotspot 33 per hazard and −10 per empty click (floor 0); order 100 if fully correct else 25 per correct slot, and a life is lost unless the whole order is right; 3 lives; timers 30/20/45/60s; pass at 700 base points.

```js
// ❌ BAD
const data = await fetch("./content.json");

// ✅ GOOD
const node = window.CONTENT.nodes[state.nodeId];
```
